<p><strong>To start a gym or fitness studio in Nepal, decide your offer, set simple membership plans, plan your trainers and class timetable, and put payments, attendance and reporting in place before opening day. Check registration, licence and tax rules with the relevant Nepali authorities.</strong></p>
<p>This is an operations guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm registration, licence, health and tax rules with the relevant authorities and your accountant.</p>
<h2>1. Decide what you are selling</h2>
<p>A full gym floor, group classes, personal training or a mix? Each needs different staffing and a different way of charging. Pick your core offer first and price it before you add extras.</p>
<h2>2. Keep membership plans simple</h2>
<p>Monthly, quarterly and yearly plans, plus a drop-in or trial pass, are enough to begin. What matters is knowing every member's plan, start date and expiry. Track them with <a href="/features/memberships/">prepaid memberships</a> so a lapsed member is visible at the door. Read <a href="/blog/gym-members-expired-still-training-nepal/">what to do when expired members keep training</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Plan trainers and classes</h2>
<p>Assign trainers to classes and sessions, and set a maximum class size. See <a href="/blog/class-capacity-limits-full-class-yoga-gym-nepal/">how class capacity limits work</a> and <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff management</a>.</p>
<h2>4. Take bookings and payments from day one</h2>
<p>Members expect to book a class or a trainer without calling. Record what was paid, how, and what is still owed. See <a href="/features/booking/">online booking</a> and <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</p>
<h2>5. Sell personal training as packages</h2>
<p>A block of sessions brings cash in early and keeps clients coming. <a href="/features/packages/">Session packages</a> show how many sessions remain.</p>
<h2>6. Set rules for discounts</h2>
<p>Launch offers are common, and so is unrecorded discounting. Decide who may discount and who approves. See <a href="/features/discount-management/">discount management</a>.</p>
<h2>7. Plan for a second branch</h2>
<p>Choose software that scales. Read the <a href="/blog/gym-management-nepal/">gym management guide</a> and the <a href="/compare/gym-software-nepal/">questions to ask every gym software vendor</a>, or see <a href="/solutions/fitness/">Zennly for gyms and fitness studios</a>.</p>
